{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nAfter the sibling story \"validity-only by default; no code path reads the repo-pinned trust file\" lands, no verification, signing, health or merge-gate path reads `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml`. The file, its loader `src/rebar/attest/trusted_env.py`, and the `rebar trusted-env` command (`src/rebar/_commands/trusted_env_cmd.py`, parser factory `build_trusted_env` in `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/certs.py`, registry rows at `src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py` lines 304 and 326, help `src/rebar/_cli/help/trusted-env.txt`) still exist. ADR 0125 removes them so no op-cert keys are pinned in the repository. Sequencing: built on the validity-only story's merged commit, which already deletes `tests/unit/test_opcert_public_counterpart_guard_879b.py` (the module that monkeypatches `rebar.attest.trusted_env`).\n\n## Approach\n1. Delete `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml`, `src/rebar/attest/trusted_env.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/trusted_env_cmd.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/help/trusted-env.txt`, and `tests/unit/test_trusted_env.py`.\n2. Remove `build_trusted_env` from `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/certs.py` (keep the `remote-cert` factory; update the module docstring), the two `trusted-env` rows from `src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py`, the `trusted-env` line from `src/rebar/_cli/help/overview.txt`, and the `trusted-env` row from `docs/exit-codes.md` (line 220; `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_exit_codes.py` pairs every documented row with a live route). In `.gitignore`: delete line 26 (`!.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml`), drop the \"but TRACK the out-of-band trusted-environment pin\" clause from the comment at lines 20-22, and reword the comment at lines 27-28 without the pin file.\n3. Tests: in `tests/interfaces/facades/test_intercept_registry_cutover_s6.py`, replace the `trusted-env` row of the registered-command table with an explicit absence test: `\"trusted-env\"` is in neither registry map of `src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py`, and `rebar trusted-env --help` exits non-zero as an unknown command. Delete `test_trusted_env_preserves_explicit_multiline_usage` (`tests/unit/test_gen_cli_help.py` line 102) and drop `trusted-env` from the tables in `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_cli_help_writing_guidelines_jerboa.py`. In `tests/unit/test_opcert_deploy_infra.py`, remove `test_trusted_env_pins_deployed_environment_log_position_form` (line 293), the module-level `from rebar.attest import trusted_env` (line 22), the `_TRUSTED_ENV` constant (line 34), its section banner, and the pinning mention in the module docstring. In `tests/unit/test_verify_opcert_ac_coverage.py`, delete section \"3. trusted-env helper\" (`test_trusted_env_add_and_revoke_stamp_tip_position`, lines 328-375) and helpers only it uses. Replace the pin-file fixture in `tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py` (lines 444-553) with the trust-list form where the test still needs trust.\n4. Regenerate `docs/cli-reference.md` (`scripts/gen_cli_reference.py`) and help artifacts (`scripts/gen_cli_help.py`), plus any census a failing drift test names. If the mechanism ratchet reports removed mechanisms as stale, run `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --update-stale` and commit the shrunk baseline.\n5. Update the docstring of `src/rebar/attest/opcert.py` (line 13), which names the pin file.\nBefore committing, re-derive the reference set with Serena `find_referencing_symbols` on `trusted_env` symbols plus `git grep -nF` for `rebar.attest.trusted_env`, `trusted_env`, `trusted-env` and `trusted_environments`, and handle any site not listed here.\n\n## Scope\n- Deleted: `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml`, `src/rebar/attest/trusted_env.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/trusted_env_cmd.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/help/trusted-env.txt`, `tests/unit/test_trusted_env.py`\n- Edited: `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/certs.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/help/overview.txt`, `.gitignore`, `src/rebar/attest/opcert.py`, `docs/exit-codes.md`, `docs/cli-reference.md`, `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` (only via `--update-stale`)\n- Tests: `tests/interfaces/facades/test_intercept_registry_cutover_s6.py`, `tests/unit/test_gen_cli_help.py`, `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_cli_help_writing_guidelines_jerboa.py`, `tests/unit/test_opcert_deploy_infra.py`, `tests/unit/test_verify_opcert_ac_coverage.py`, `tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py`\nOut of scope: prose docs and runbooks (docs sibling); historical ADRs 0049, 0098, 0100, 0104 keep their text; eval corpora and fixtures under `evals/` and `tests/fixtures/` that quote the filename as data.\n\n## Testing\nRemoval only; the behaviour change already landed. The new absence test in `test_intercept_registry_cutover_s6.py` fails on the parent commit (command registered) and passes after the deletion. Help and reference artifacts regenerate without `trusted-env`; `make verify` passes. Portability: deletions and a pure-Python registry assertion.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `git ls-files .rebar/trusted_environments.yaml src/rebar/attest/trusted_env.py src/rebar/_commands/trusted_env_cmd.py src/rebar/_cli/help/trusted-env.txt tests/unit/test_trusted_env.py` prints nothing.\n- [x] `git grep -nF trusted_environments -- src` and `git grep -nF trusted_env -- src` print no hits.\n- [x] The absence test passes: `trusted-env` is not in the CLI registry and `rebar trusted-env --help` exits non-zero (checked: `pytest tests/interfaces/facades/test_intercept_registry_cutover_s6.py -q`).\n- [x] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0.\n- [x] `make verify` is green, and the change lands through Gerrit with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1795210386082271001,"uuid":"43d1540a-0b1c-4833-84c9-86ba9de3b2c1"}